51	40	15	O	Woodcutters	https://codeforces.com/problemset/problem/545/C	{"meta": {"title": "C. Woodcutters", "timeLimit": "1 second", "memoryLimit": "256 megabytes"}, "type": "problem", "story": "<div class=\\"header\\"><div class=\\"title\\">C. Woodcutters</div><div class=\\"time-limit\\"><div class=\\"property-title\\">time limit per test</div>1 second</div><div class=\\"memory-limit\\"><div class=\\"property-title\\">memory limit per test</div>256 megabytes</div><div class=\\"input-file input-standard\\"><div class=\\"property-title\\">input</div>standard input</div><div class=\\"output-file output-standard\\"><div class=\\"property-title\\">output</div>standard output</div></div><div><p>Little Susie listens to fairy tales before bed every day. Today's fairy tale was about wood cutters and the little girl immediately started imagining the choppers cutting wood. She imagined the situation that is described below.</p><p>There are <span class=\\"tex-span\\"><i>n</i></span> trees located along the road at points with coordinates <span class=\\"tex-span\\"><i>x</i><sub class=\\"lower-index\\">1</sub>, <i>x</i><sub class=\\"lower-index\\">2</sub>, ..., <i>x</i><sub class=\\"lower-index\\"><i>n</i></sub></span>. Each tree has its height <span class=\\"tex-span\\"><i>h</i><sub class=\\"lower-index\\"><i>i</i></sub></span>. Woodcutters can cut down a tree and fell it to the left or to the right. After that it occupies one of the segments <span class=\\"tex-span\\">[<i>x</i><sub class=\\"lower-index\\"><i>i</i></sub> - <i>h</i><sub class=\\"lower-index\\"><i>i</i></sub>, <i>x</i><sub class=\\"lower-index\\"><i>i</i></sub>]</span> or <span class=\\"tex-span\\">[<i>x</i><sub class=\\"lower-index\\"><i>i</i></sub>;<i>x</i><sub class=\\"lower-index\\"><i>i</i></sub> + <i>h</i><sub class=\\"lower-index\\"><i>i</i></sub>]</span>. The tree that is not cut down occupies a single point with coordinate <span class=\\"tex-span\\"><i>x</i><sub class=\\"lower-index\\"><i>i</i></sub></span>. Woodcutters can fell a tree if the segment to be occupied by the fallen tree doesn't contain any occupied point. The woodcutters want to process as many trees as possible, so Susie wonders, what is the maximum number of trees to fell. </p></div><div class=\\"input-specification\\"><div class=\\"section-title\\">Input</div><p>The first line contains integer <span class=\\"tex-span\\"><i>n</i></span> (<span class=\\"tex-span\\">1 ≤ <i>n</i> ≤ 10<sup class=\\"upper-index\\">5</sup></span>) — the number of trees.</p><p>Next <span class=\\"tex-span\\"><i>n</i></span> lines contain pairs of integers <span class=\\"tex-span\\"><i>x</i><sub class=\\"lower-index\\"><i>i</i></sub>, <i>h</i><sub class=\\"lower-index\\"><i>i</i></sub></span> (<span class=\\"tex-span\\">1 ≤ <i>x</i><sub class=\\"lower-index\\"><i>i</i></sub>, <i>h</i><sub class=\\"lower-index\\"><i>i</i></sub> ≤ 10<sup class=\\"upper-index\\">9</sup></span>) — the coordinate and the height of the <span class=\\"tex-span\\"><i>і</i></span>-th tree.</p><p>The pairs are given in the order of ascending <span class=\\"tex-span\\"><i>x</i><sub class=\\"lower-index\\"><i>i</i></sub></span>. No two trees are located at the point with the same coordinate.</p></div><div class=\\"output-specification\\"><div class=\\"section-title\\">Output</div><p>Print a single number — the maximum number of trees that you can cut down by the given rules.</p></div><div class=\\"sample-tests\\"><div class=\\"section-title\\">Examples</div><div class=\\"sample-test\\"><div class=\\"input\\"><div class=\\"title\\">Input<div title=\\"Copy\\" data-clipboard-target=\\"#id008316104215995361\\" id=\\"id003182702843274203\\" class=\\"input-output-copier\\">Copy</div></div><pre id=\\"id008316104215995361\\">5<br>1 2<br>2 1<br>5 10<br>10 9<br>19 1<br></pre></div><div class=\\"output\\"><div class=\\"title\\">Output<div title=\\"Copy\\" data-clipboard-target=\\"#id0037511740885692246\\" id=\\"id0008203925401362544\\" class=\\"input-output-copier\\">Copy</div></div><pre id=\\"id0037511740885692246\\">3<br></pre></div><div class=\\"input\\"><div class=\\"title\\">Input<div title=\\"Copy\\" data-clipboard-target=\\"#id009907290379767777\\" id=\\"id0018524894481538978\\" class=\\"input-output-copier\\">Copy</div></div><pre id=\\"id009907290379767777\\">5<br>1 2<br>2 1<br>5 10<br>10 9<br>20 1<br></pre></div><div class=\\"output\\"><div class=\\"title\\">Output<div title=\\"Copy\\" data-clipboard-target=\\"#id00512513079666784\\" id=\\"id0020431883264629436\\" class=\\"input-output-copier\\">Copy</div></div><pre id=\\"id00512513079666784\\">4<br></pre></div></div></div><div class=\\"note\\"><div class=\\"section-title\\">Note</div><p>In the first sample you can fell the trees like that: </p><ul> <li> fell the <span class=\\"tex-span\\">1</span>-st tree to the left — now it occupies segment <span class=\\"tex-span\\">[ - 1;1]</span> </li><li> fell the <span class=\\"tex-span\\">2</span>-nd tree to the right — now it occupies segment <span class=\\"tex-span\\">[2;3]</span> </li><li> leave the <span class=\\"tex-span\\">3</span>-rd tree — it occupies point <span class=\\"tex-span\\">5</span> </li><li> leave the <span class=\\"tex-span\\">4</span>-th tree — it occupies point <span class=\\"tex-span\\">10</span> </li><li> fell the <span class=\\"tex-span\\">5</span>-th tree to the right — now it occupies segment <span class=\\"tex-span\\">[19;20]</span> </li></ul><p>In the second sample you can also fell <span class=\\"tex-span\\">4</span>-th tree to the right, after that it will occupy segment <span class=\\"tex-span\\">[10;19]</span>.</p></div>", "testCases": []}	\N	1500	\N
52	17	1	A	PUBG Analysis	https://codeforces.com/group/E23MsQv91X/contest/315226/problem/A	{"meta": {"title": "A. PUBG Analysis", "inputType": "standard input", "timeLimit": "2 seconds", "outputType": "standard output", "memoryLimit": "1024 megabytes", "timeLimitMs": 2000, "memoryLimitMB": 1024}, "note": "<p>-if <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(U1\\\\)</span> Beat <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(U2\\\\)</span> and <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(U2\\\\)</span> was stand on his foot, so <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(U2\\\\)</span> can't knock or kill anyone until he will be Revivied.</p><p>-if <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(U1\\\\)</span> Beat <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(U2\\\\)</span> and <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(U2\\\\)</span> was knocked, so <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(U2\\\\)</span> is out of the room and can't do any actions, and <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(U1\\\\)</span>'s team gets one kill.</p><p>-if <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(U1\\\\)</span>, <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(U2\\\\)</span> and <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(U3\\\\)</span> aren't in the same team: if <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(U1\\\\)</span> Beat <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(U2\\\\)</span> and <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(U2\\\\)</span> was stand on his foot, and <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(U3\\\\)</span> Beat <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(U2\\\\)</span> and <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(U2\\\\)</span> was knocked, so the kill goes to <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(U3\\\\)</span>'s team.</p><p>-if <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(U1\\\\)</span> beat all <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(U3\\\\)</span>'s team, his team didn't take the kills which <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(U3\\\\)</span>'s team have.</p><p>-if <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(U1\\\\)</span> and <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(U2\\\\)</span> in the same team, they can't Beat each other.</p><p>-if <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(U1\\\\)</span> is knocked, he can't Revive himself, Should one of his team who stand on his foot Revive him.</p>", "type": "problem", "story": "<div><p>It's time to get the \\"Winner Winner Chicken Dinner!!\\", <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(Now\\\\)</span> <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(let's\\\\)</span> <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(Play\\\\)</span> !!</p><center> <img class=\\"tex-graphics\\" src=\\"https://espresso.codeforces.com/658de4a007ca7c7422d4175fa45e10a2f82495c9.png\\" style=\\"max-width: 100.0%;max-height: 100.0%;\\"> </center><p>You have a <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(Room\\\\)</span> <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(Card\\\\)</span> and you invite <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\((N\\\\)</span> x <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(4)\\\\)</span> friends to paly in your room.</p><p>you will be given the <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(UserName\\\\)</span> of each of your friends, and <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(M\\\\)</span> commands that describe what will happen in the room.</p><p>in each Command you will be given <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(Three\\\\)</span> strings <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(U1\\\\)</span>, <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(X\\\\)</span>, <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(U2\\\\)</span>.</p><p><span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(U1\\\\)</span> and <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(U2\\\\)</span> is a <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(UserName\\\\)</span>.</p><p><span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(X\\\\)</span> is one of the following actions (\\"Beat\\", \\"Revive\\").</p><p>- <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(U1\\\\)</span> beat <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(U2\\\\)</span> : That's mean <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(U1\\\\)</span> kill or knock <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(U2\\\\)</span> (<span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(knock\\\\)</span> if there is other player stand in his squad, <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(kill\\\\)</span> if <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(U2\\\\)</span> is the last one stand in his Squad or <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(U2\\\\)</span> has been knocked), (<span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(U1\\\\)</span> and <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(U2\\\\)</span> isn't in the same squad)</p><p>- <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(U1\\\\)</span> Revive <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(U2\\\\)</span> : That's mean <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(U1\\\\)</span> get back <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(U2\\\\)</span> to stand after getting knocked (<span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(U1\\\\)</span> and <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(U2\\\\)</span> is in the same squad).</p><p>You as an Analyst you will give a report that describe how many kills that each squad have.</p><p>You must make a program to help you with that, Can you ?</p></div>", "inputSpec": "<p>In the first line you will be given an integer <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(N\\\\)</span> (the number of squads in the room). <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\((2 \\\\le N \\\\le 25)\\\\)</span> In the next <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(N\\\\)</span> lines, in each line there will be <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(Four\\\\)</span> strings, the <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(UserName\\\\)</span> of the players in the <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(i_t\\\\)</span><span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(_h\\\\)</span> squad (the UserName of all the players are distinct).</p><p>Then you will be given an integer <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(M\\\\)</span> (the number of commands) <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\((2 \\\\le M \\\\le N*4)\\\\)</span>.</p><p>In the <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(i_t\\\\)</span><span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(_h\\\\)</span> command you will get <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(Three\\\\)</span> strings <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(U1\\\\)</span> <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(X\\\\)</span> <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(U2\\\\)</span>.</p><p><span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(U1\\\\)</span> and <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(U2\\\\)</span> is a <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(UserName\\\\)</span>.</p><p><span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(X\\\\)</span> is the <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(Actions\\\\)</span>.</p>", "testCases": [{"id": 1, "input": "3\\nHussien Ezzat Karemo Hawary\\nHafiz Hamdy Shehata Ashour\\nKareem Ramy Fahmy Omar\\n11\\nHussien Beat Hamdy\\nEzzat Beat Hafiz\\nOmar Beat Shehata\\nAshour Beat Karemo\\nAshour Revive Hafiz\\nAshour Beat Karemo\\nRamy Beat Ashour\\nKareem Beat Hafiz\\nFahmy Beat Hussien\\nOmar Beat Hawary\\nRamy Beat Ezzat", "output": "1 1 6"}], "outputSpec": "<p>Print an Array <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(A\\\\)</span> of <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(N\\\\)</span> integers separated by spaces which the <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(A_i\\\\)</span> is the number of kills that the <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(i_t\\\\)</span><span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(_h\\\\)</span> squad have.</p>"}	\N	\N	315226
