138	3	24	X	8 Neighbors	https://codeforces.com/group/MWSDmqGsZm/contest/219774/problem/X	{"meta": {"title": "X. 8 Neighbors", "inputType": "standard input", "timeLimit": "1 second", "outputType": "standard output", "memoryLimit": "256 megabytes", "timeLimitMs": 1000, "memoryLimitMB": 256}, "note": null, "type": "problem", "story": "<div><p>Given two numbers <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(N\\\\)</span> and <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(M\\\\)</span>, a 2D array <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(A\\\\)</span> of size <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(N\\\\)</span> * <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(M\\\\)</span> which contains 'x' or '.' only and two numbers <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(X\\\\)</span>, <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(Y\\\\)</span> which donates a cell position in <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(A\\\\)</span> such that <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(X\\\\)</span> is the row number and <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(Y\\\\)</span> is the column number.</p><p>Determine whether all neighbors of the given cell are 'x' or not.</p><p><span class=\\"tex-font-style-bf\\">Note:</span> The neighbor cell is any cell that shares an <span class=\\"tex-font-style-bf\\">edge</span> or a <span class=\\"tex-font-style-bf\\">corner</span> and it should be <span class=\\"tex-font-style-bf\\">inside</span> 2D array.</p><center> <img class=\\"tex-graphics\\" src=\\"https://espresso.codeforces.com/84c6dfb0d33a18bb2897464f6dc5d3968484a66c.png\\" style=\\"max-width: 100.0%;max-height: 100.0%;\\"> </center> </div>", "inputSpec": "<p>First line contains two numbers <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(N\\\\)</span>, <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(M\\\\)</span> <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\((2 \\\\le N,M \\\\le 100)\\\\)</span> <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(N\\\\)</span> donates number of rows and <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(M\\\\)</span> donates number of columns.</p><p>Each of the next <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(N\\\\)</span> lines will contain <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(M\\\\)</span> symbol can be ('.' or 'x').</p><p>Last line contains two numbers <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(X\\\\)</span>, <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(Y\\\\)</span> <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\((1 \\\\le X \\\\le N, 1 \\\\le Y \\\\le M)\\\\)</span>.</p>", "testCases": [{"id": 1, "input": "3 3\\nxxx\\nx.x\\nxxx\\n2 2", "output": "yes"}, {"id": 2, "input": "3 3\\nxxx\\nxxx\\nxx.\\n2 2", "output": "no"}, {"id": 3, "input": "3 3\\nxxx\\nxxx\\nxxx\\n1 1", "output": "yes"}], "outputSpec": "<p>Print \\"<span class=\\"tex-font-style-bf\\">yes</span>\\" if all neighbors of the given cell are 'x' otherwise, print \\"<span class=\\"tex-font-style-bf\\">no</span>\\" without quotations.</p>"}	\N	800	219774
