143	38	15	O	System Administrator	https://codeforces.com/problemset/problem/22/C	{"meta": {"title": "C. System Administrator", "timeLimit": "1 second", "memoryLimit": "256 megabytes"}, "type": "problem", "story": "<div class=\\"header\\"><div class=\\"title\\">C. System Administrator</div><div class=\\"time-limit\\"><div class=\\"property-title\\">time limit per test</div>1 second</div><div class=\\"memory-limit\\"><div class=\\"property-title\\">memory limit per test</div>256 megabytes</div><div class=\\"input-file input-standard\\" style=\\"font-weight: bold\\"><div class=\\"property-title\\">input</div>stdin</div><div class=\\"output-file output-standard\\" style=\\"font-weight: bold\\"><div class=\\"property-title\\">output</div>stdout</div></div><div><p>Bob got a job as a system administrator in X corporation. His first task was to connect <span class=\\"tex-span\\"><i>n</i></span> servers with the help of <span class=\\"tex-span\\"><i>m</i></span> two-way direct connection so that it becomes possible to transmit data from one server to any other server via these connections. Each direct connection has to link two different servers, each pair of servers should have at most one direct connection. Y corporation, a business rival of X corporation, made Bob an offer that he couldn't refuse: Bob was asked to connect the servers in such a way, that when server with index <span class=\\"tex-span\\"><i>v</i></span> fails, the transmission of data between some other two servers becomes impossible, i.e. the system stops being connected. Help Bob connect the servers.</p></div><div class=\\"input-specification\\"><div class=\\"section-title\\">Input</div><p>The first input line contains 3 space-separated integer numbers <span class=\\"tex-span\\"><i>n</i></span>, <span class=\\"tex-span\\"><i>m</i></span>, <span class=\\"tex-span\\"><i>v</i></span> (<span class=\\"tex-span\\">3 ≤ <i>n</i> ≤ 10<sup class=\\"upper-index\\">5</sup>, 0 ≤ <i>m</i> ≤ 10<sup class=\\"upper-index\\">5</sup>, 1 ≤ <i>v</i> ≤ <i>n</i></span>), <span class=\\"tex-span\\"><i>n</i></span> — amount of servers, <span class=\\"tex-span\\"><i>m</i></span> — amount of direct connections, <span class=\\"tex-span\\"><i>v</i></span> — index of the server that fails and leads to the failure of the whole system.</p></div><div class=\\"output-specification\\"><div class=\\"section-title\\">Output</div><p>If it is impossible to connect the servers in the required way, output <span class=\\"tex-font-style-tt\\">-1</span>. Otherwise output <span class=\\"tex-span\\"><i>m</i></span> lines with 2 numbers each — description of all the direct connections in the system. Each direct connection is described by two numbers — indexes of two servers, linked by this direct connection. The servers are numbered from 1. If the answer is not unique, output any.</p></div><div class=\\"sample-tests\\"><div class=\\"section-title\\">Examples</div><div class=\\"sample-test\\"><div class=\\"input\\"><div class=\\"title\\">Input<div title=\\"Copy\\" data-clipboard-target=\\"#id008167809035375782\\" id=\\"id005158354543024839\\" class=\\"input-output-copier\\">Copy</div></div><pre id=\\"id008167809035375782\\">5 6 3<br></pre></div><div class=\\"output\\"><div class=\\"title\\">Output<div title=\\"Copy\\" data-clipboard-target=\\"#id006925088038500182\\" id=\\"id00440845998758683\\" class=\\"input-output-copier\\">Copy</div></div><pre id=\\"id006925088038500182\\">1 2<br>2 3<br>3 4<br>4 5<br>1 3<br>3 5<br></pre></div><div class=\\"input\\"><div class=\\"title\\">Input<div title=\\"Copy\\" data-clipboard-target=\\"#id007804727583979456\\" id=\\"id007808999349345942\\" class=\\"input-output-copier\\">Copy</div></div><pre id=\\"id007804727583979456\\">6 100 1<br></pre></div><div class=\\"output\\"><div class=\\"title\\">Output<div title=\\"Copy\\" data-clipboard-target=\\"#id0048638874136649823\\" id=\\"id0025282025142672815\\" class=\\"input-output-copier\\">Copy</div></div><pre id=\\"id0048638874136649823\\">-1<br></pre></div></div></div>", "testCases": []}	\N	1700	\N
178	10	24	X	Strange Addition	https://codeforces.com/group/MWSDmqGsZm/contest/223340/problem/X	{"meta": {"title": "X. Strange Addition", "inputType": "stdin", "timeLimit": "2 seconds", "outputType": "stdout", "memoryLimit": "256 megabytes", "timeLimitMs": 2000, "memoryLimitMB": 256}, "note": null, "type": "problem", "story": "<div><p>Unfortunately, Vasya can only sum pairs of integers (<span class=\\"tex-span\\"><i>a</i></span>, <span class=\\"tex-span\\"><i>b</i></span>), such that for any decimal place at least one number has digit <span class=\\"tex-span\\">0</span> in this place. For example, Vasya can sum numbers <span class=\\"tex-span\\">505</span> and <span class=\\"tex-span\\">50</span>, but he cannot sum <span class=\\"tex-span\\">1</span> and <span class=\\"tex-span\\">4</span>.</p><p>Vasya has a set of <span class=\\"tex-span\\"><i>k</i></span> distinct non-negative integers <span class=\\"tex-span\\"><i>d</i><sub class=\\"lower-index\\">1</sub>, <i>d</i><sub class=\\"lower-index\\">2</sub>, ..., <i>d</i><sub class=\\"lower-index\\"><i>k</i></sub></span>.</p><p>Vasya wants to choose some integers from this set so that he could sum any two chosen numbers. What maximal number of integers can he choose in the required manner?</p></div>", "inputSpec": "<p>The first input line contains integer <span class=\\"tex-span\\"><i>k</i></span> <span class=\\"tex-span\\">(1 ≤ <i>k</i> ≤ 100)</span> — the number of integers.</p><p>The second line contains <span class=\\"tex-span\\"><i>k</i></span> distinct space-separated integers <span class=\\"tex-span\\"><i>d</i><sub class=\\"lower-index\\">1</sub>, <i>d</i><sub class=\\"lower-index\\">2</sub>, ..., <i>d</i><sub class=\\"lower-index\\"><i>k</i></sub></span> <span class=\\"tex-span\\">(0 ≤ <i>d</i><sub class=\\"lower-index\\"><i>i</i></sub> ≤ 100)</span>.</p>", "testCases": [{"id": 1, "input": "4\\n100 10 1 0", "output": "4\\n0 1 10 100"}, {"id": 2, "input": "3\\n2 70 3", "output": "2\\n2 70"}], "outputSpec": "<p>In the first line print a single integer <span class=\\"tex-span\\"><i>n</i></span> the maximum number of the chosen integers. In the second line print <span class=\\"tex-span\\"><i>n</i></span> distinct non-negative integers — the required integers.</p><p>If there are multiple solutions, print any of them. You can print the numbers in any order.</p>"}	\N	1600	223340
144	15	1	A	Play With Ezzat	https://codeforces.com/group/E23MsQv91X/contest/317001/problem/A	{"meta": {"title": "A. Play With Ezzat", "inputType": "standard input", "timeLimit": "1 second", "outputType": "standard output", "memoryLimit": "256 megabytes", "timeLimitMs": 1000, "memoryLimitMB": 256}, "note": null, "type": "problem", "story": "<div><p>Ezzat do not like waste your time then there is a problem directly.</p><p> There is a string <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(s\\\\)</span> of length 3 or greater. No two neighboring characters in <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(s\\\\)</span> are equal.</p><p>Ezzat and MaTb3aa will play a game against each other. The two players alternately performs the following operation, Ezzat going first:</p><p>Remove one of the characters in s, excluding both ends. However, a character cannot be removed if removal of the character would result in two neighboring equal characters in s.</p><p>The player who becomes unable to perform the operation, loses the game. Determine which player will win when the two play optimally.</p></div>", "inputSpec": "<p>The input is given from Standard Input in the following format:</p><p>(<span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(3 \\\\le |s| \\\\le 10^5\\\\)</span>) s consists of lowercase English letters.</p><p>No two neighboring characters in s are equal.</p>", "testCases": [{"id": 1, "input": "aba", "output": "MaTb3aa"}, {"id": 2, "input": "abcab", "output": "Ezzat"}], "outputSpec": "<p>If Ezzat will win, print \\"Ezzat\\". If MaTb3aa will win, print \\"MaTb3aa\\".</p>"}	\N	\N	317001
145	5	2	B	Print	https://codeforces.com/group/MWSDmqGsZm/contest/223205/problem/B	{"meta": {"title": "B. Print", "inputType": "standard input", "timeLimit": "1 second", "outputType": "standard output", "memoryLimit": "64 megabytes", "timeLimitMs": 1000, "memoryLimitMB": 64}, "note": "<p>Don't use any leading or trilling spaces.</p>", "type": "problem", "story": "<div><p>Given a number <span class=\\"tex-span\\"><i>N</i></span>. Print all numbers from <span class=\\"tex-font-style-bf\\">1</span> to <span class=\\"tex-span\\"><i>N</i></span>.</p><p><span class=\\"tex-font-style-bf\\">Note:</span> Solve this problem using function.</p></div>", "inputSpec": "<p>Only one line contains a number <span class=\\"tex-span\\"><i>N</i></span> <span class=\\"tex-span\\">(1 ≤ <i>N</i> ≤ 10<sup class=\\"upper-index\\">3</sup>)</span>.</p>", "testCases": [{"id": 1, "input": "5", "output": "1 2 3 4 5"}], "outputSpec": "<p>print numbers form <span class=\\"tex-font-style-bf\\">1</span> to <span class=\\"tex-span\\"><i>N</i></span> separated by a single space.</p>"}	\N	800	223205
146	6	4	D	Xor	https://codeforces.com/group/MWSDmqGsZm/contest/223338/problem/D	{"meta": {"title": "D. Xor", "inputType": "standard input", "timeLimit": "1 second", "outputType": "standard output", "memoryLimit": "256 megabytes", "timeLimitMs": 1000, "memoryLimitMB": 256}, "note": "<p>In c++ to use xor operator you may write :</p><p>int x = a ^ b;</p><p>but if you need to print a ^ b</p><p>you should write</p><p>cout « (a ^ b);</p>", "type": "problem", "story": "<div><p>Given three numbers <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(A\\\\)</span>, <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(B\\\\)</span> and <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(Q\\\\)</span>. Determine the value of the <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(Q_{th}\\\\)</span> element using the formula below: <img class=\\"tex-graphics\\" src=\\"https://espresso.codeforces.com/e2793afb91f6be34ba73d661279533e653064c46.png\\" style=\\"max-width: 100.0%;max-height: 100.0%;\\"></p></div>", "inputSpec": "<p>Only one line contains three numbers <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(A\\\\)</span>, <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(B\\\\)</span> and <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(Q\\\\)</span> <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\((1 \\\\le A, B, Q \\\\le 10^{12})\\\\)</span>.</p>", "testCases": [{"id": 1, "input": "5 3 1", "output": "5"}, {"id": 2, "input": "5 3 2", "output": "3"}, {"id": 3, "input": "5 3 3", "output": "6"}], "outputSpec": "<p>Print the value of the <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(Q_{th}\\\\)</span> element.</p>"}	\N	2000	223338
147	14	3	C	Tic Tac Toe	https://codeforces.com/group/E23MsQv91X/contest/318121/problem/C	{"meta": {"title": "C. Tic Tac Toe", "inputType": "standard input", "timeLimit": "2 seconds", "outputType": "standard output", "memoryLimit": "64 megabytes", "timeLimitMs": 2000, "memoryLimitMB": 64}, "note": "<p>In First example no one will win and game can be as following : </p><center> <img class=\\"tex-graphics\\" src=\\"https://espresso.codeforces.com/e15085d65e7c692712909816e3d7cddc7569db66.png\\" style=\\"max-width: 100.0%;max-height: 100.0%;\\"> </center> <center> .................................................................................... </center> <center> <img class=\\"tex-graphics\\" src=\\"https://espresso.codeforces.com/2731aa64a43a8233edb264eaa1e25327efc0e705.png\\" style=\\"max-width: 100.0%;max-height: 100.0%;\\"> </center> <center> .................................................................................... </center><center> <img class=\\"tex-graphics\\" src=\\"https://espresso.codeforces.com/f0c546c57b7576ed45c35263ef51259b2325da14.png\\" style=\\"max-width: 100.0%;max-height: 100.0%;\\"> </center> <center> .................................................................................... </center><center> <img class=\\"tex-graphics\\" src=\\"https://espresso.codeforces.com/be3c00549cd14aa5492e8cb55e4f4d598a468e8b.png\\" style=\\"max-width: 100.0%;max-height: 100.0%;\\"> </center> <center> .................................................................................... </center><center> <img class=\\"tex-graphics\\" src=\\"https://espresso.codeforces.com/edabdc8b485624b7fa1772ddac47b35e9f392dac.png\\" style=\\"max-width: 100.0%;max-height: 100.0%;\\"> </center>", "type": "problem", "story": "<div><p>On a hot day in Assuit , Nada is bored , so she tell khloud to play a game with her the game is called Tic Tac Toe.</p><p>Tic Tac Toe is a child's game played on a 3 by 3 grid. One player, X, starts by placing an X at an unoccupied grid position. Then the other player, O, places an O at an unoccupied grid position. Play alternates between X and O until the grid is filled or one player's symbols occupy an entire line (vertical, horizontal, or diagonal) in the grid.</p><p>The game is played on the square field 3 X 3. Let us suppose that the cells are numerated in the following way:</p><center> <img class=\\"tex-graphics\\" src=\\"https://espresso.codeforces.com/a43b8c6c30535076103af2a01eb867f3bcad1e6a.png\\" style=\\"max-width: 100.0%;max-height: 100.0%;\\"> </center><p>two players put their marks (X for first and O for second) in turns into any of free cells remaining. One who completes the straight line of three marks (three X-s or three O-s) immediately wins. Lines could be filled either in rows or columns or one of two diagonals (8 lines possible in total)</p><p>Nada and khloud will play perfect. If Nada is the first player to move and you will given which cell he choose first, predict the winner of this game or game will end with draw ?.</p></div>", "inputSpec": "<p> Only one line an integern (1&lt;=n&lt;=9) position that Nada will choose to play first .</p>", "testCases": [{"id": 1, "input": "5", "output": "draw"}], "outputSpec": "<p>Print \\"Nada\\" if Nada will win , print \\"khloud\\" if khloud will win , otherwise print \\"draw\\".</p>"}	\N	\N	318121
