233	28	4	D	CDs	https://codeforces.com/group/3nQaj5GMG5/contest/374321/problem/D	{"meta": {"title": "D. CDs", "inputType": "standard input", "timeLimit": "1 second", "outputType": "standard output", "memoryLimit": "256 megabytes", "timeLimitMs": 1000, "memoryLimitMB": 256}, "note": null, "type": "problem", "story": "<div><p>Jack and Jill have decided to sell some of their Compact Discs, while they still have some value. They have decided to sell one of each of the CD titles that they both own.</p><p>How many CDs can Jack and Jill sell? Neither Jack nor Jill owns more than one copy of each CD.</p></div>", "inputSpec": "<p>The first line of the input contains two integers <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(N\\\\)</span> and <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(M\\\\)</span> <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\((1 \\\\leq N, M \\\\leq 10^6)\\\\)</span> — The number of CDs owned by Jack and by Jill, respectively.</p><p>The second line contains <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(N\\\\)</span> space-separated integers <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\((1 \\\\leq a_i \\\\leq 10^9)\\\\)</span> — the catalog numbers of the CDs owned by Jack.</p><p>The third line contains <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(M\\\\)</span> space-separated integers <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\((1 \\\\leq b_i \\\\leq 10^9)\\\\)</span> — the catalog numbers of the CDs owned by Jill.</p>", "testCases": [{"id": 1, "input": "3 3\\n1 2 3\\n1 2 4", "output": "2"}], "outputSpec": "<p>Print a single integer — The number of CDs Jack and Jill can sell.</p>"}	\N	\N	374321
