272	21	6	F	Create The Teams	https://codeforces.com/group/E23MsQv91X/contest/311232/problem/F	{"meta": {"title": "F. Create The Teams", "inputType": "standard input", "timeLimit": "2 seconds", "outputType": "standard output", "memoryLimit": "256 megabytes", "timeLimitMs": 2000, "memoryLimitMB": 256}, "note": null, "type": "problem", "story": "<div><p>There are <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(n\\\\)</span> programmers that you want to split into several non-empty teams. The skill of the <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(i\\\\)</span>-th programmer is <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(a_i\\\\)</span>. You want to assemble the maximum number of teams from them. There is a restriction for each team: the number of programmers in the team multiplied by the minimum skill among all programmers in the team must be at least <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(x\\\\)</span>.</p><p>Each programmer should belong to at most one team. Some programmers may be left without a team.</p><p>Calculate the maximum number of teams that you can assemble.</p></div>", "inputSpec": "<p>The first line contains the integer <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(t\\\\)</span> (<span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(1 \\\\le t \\\\le 1000\\\\)</span>)&nbsp;— the number of test cases.</p><p>The first line of each test case contains two integers <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(n\\\\)</span> and <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(x\\\\)</span> (<span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(1 \\\\le n \\\\le 10^5; 1 \\\\le x \\\\le 10^9\\\\)</span>)&nbsp;— the number of programmers and the restriction of team skill respectively.</p><p>The second line of each test case contains <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(n\\\\)</span> integers <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(a_1, a_2, \\\\dots , a_n\\\\)</span> (<span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(1 \\\\le a_i \\\\le 10^9\\\\)</span>), where <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(a_i\\\\)</span> is the skill of the <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(i\\\\)</span>-th programmer.</p><p>The sum of <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(n\\\\)</span> over all inputs does not exceed <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(10^5\\\\)</span>.</p>", "testCases": [{"id": 1, "input": "3\\n5 10\\n7 11 2 9 5\\n4 8\\n2 4 2 3\\n4 11\\n1 3 3 7", "output": "2\\n1\\n0"}], "outputSpec": "<p>For each test case print one integer — the maximum number of teams that you can assemble. </p>"}	\N	1400	311232
273	1	2	B	Basic Data Types	https://codeforces.com/group/MWSDmqGsZm/contest/219158/problem/B	{"meta": {"title": "B. Basic Data Types", "inputType": "standard input", "timeLimit": "1 second", "outputType": "standard output", "memoryLimit": "256 megabytes", "timeLimitMs": 1000, "memoryLimitMB": 256}, "note": null, "type": "problem", "story": "<div><p>The following lines show some C++ data types, their format specifiers and their most common bit widths:</p><ul> <li> <span class=\\"tex-font-style-bf\\">int</span> : 32 Bit integer. </li><li> <span class=\\"tex-font-style-bf\\">long long</span> : 64 bit integer </li><li> <span class=\\"tex-font-style-bf\\">Char</span> : 8 bit Characters &amp; symbols </li><li> <span class=\\"tex-font-style-bf\\">Float</span> : 32 bit real value </li><li> <span class=\\"tex-font-style-bf\\">Double</span> : 64 bit real value </li></ul><p><span class=\\"tex-font-style-bf\\">Reading</span></p><p>To read a data type, use the following syntax: </p><pre class=\\"lstlisting\\"><code class=\\"prettyprint prettyprinted\\" style=\\"\\"><span class=\\"pln\\">   cin </span><span class=\\"pun\\">&gt;&gt;</span><span class=\\"pln\\"> </span><span class=\\"typ\\">VariableName</span><span class=\\"pun\\">;</span><br><span class=\\"pln\\"> </span></code></pre> For example, to read a character followed by a double:<p> </p><pre class=\\"lstlisting\\"><code class=\\"prettyprint prettyprinted\\" style=\\"\\"><span class=\\"pln\\">  </span><span class=\\"kwd\\">char</span><span class=\\"pln\\"> ch</span><span class=\\"pun\\">;</span><br><span class=\\"pln\\">  </span><span class=\\"kwd\\">double</span><span class=\\"pln\\"> d</span><span class=\\"pun\\">;</span><br><span class=\\"pln\\">  cin </span><span class=\\"pun\\">&gt;&gt;</span><span class=\\"pln\\"> ch </span><span class=\\"pun\\">&gt;&gt;</span><span class=\\"pln\\"> d</span><span class=\\"pun\\">;</span><br><span class=\\"pln\\"> </span></code></pre><p><span class=\\"tex-font-style-bf\\">Printing</span></p><p>To print a data type, use the following syntax: </p><pre class=\\"lstlisting\\"><code class=\\"prettyprint prettyprinted\\" style=\\"\\"><span class=\\"pln\\">cout </span><span class=\\"pun\\">&lt;&lt;</span><span class=\\"pln\\"> </span><span class=\\"typ\\">VariableName</span><span class=\\"pun\\">;</span><br><span class=\\"pln\\"> </span></code></pre> For example, to print a character followed by a double:<pre class=\\"lstlisting\\"><code class=\\"prettyprint prettyprinted\\" style=\\"\\"><span class=\\"kwd\\">char</span><span class=\\"pln\\"> ch </span><span class=\\"pun\\">=</span><span class=\\"pln\\"> </span><span class=\\"str\\">'d'</span><span class=\\"pun\\">;</span><br><span class=\\"kwd\\">double</span><span class=\\"pln\\"> d </span><span class=\\"pun\\">=</span><span class=\\"pln\\"> </span><span class=\\"lit\\">234.432</span><span class=\\"pun\\">;</span><br><span class=\\"pln\\">cout </span><span class=\\"pun\\">&lt;&lt;</span><span class=\\"pln\\"> ch </span><span class=\\"pun\\">&lt;&lt;</span><span class=\\"pln\\"> </span><span class=\\"str\\">\\" \\"</span><span class=\\"pun\\">&lt;&lt;</span><span class=\\"pln\\"> d</span><span class=\\"pun\\">;</span><br><span class=\\"pln\\"> </span></code></pre></div>", "inputSpec": "<p>Only one line containing the following space-separated values: <span class=\\"tex-font-style-bf\\">int, long long, char, float</span> and <span class=\\"tex-font-style-bf\\">double</span> respectively.</p>", "testCases": [{"id": 1, "input": "3 12345678912345 a 334.23 14049.30493", "output": "3\\n12345678912345\\na\\n334.23\\n14049.3"}], "outputSpec": "<p>Print each element on a <span class=\\"tex-font-style-bf\\">new line</span> in the same order it was received as input.</p><p><span class=\\"tex-font-style-bf\\">Don't print any extra spaces</span>.</p>"}	https://drive.google.com/file/d/12EeTho38V0UPze1pvCB4NpWPEf0dthJk/view	800	219158
274	34	19	S	Permutation	https://codeforces.com/group/3nQaj5GMG5/contest/372026/problem/S	{"meta": {"title": "S. Permutation", "inputType": "mex.in", "timeLimit": "2 seconds", "outputType": "standard output", "memoryLimit": "256 megabytes", "timeLimitMs": 2000, "memoryLimitMB": 256}, "note": null, "type": "problem", "story": "<div><p>Moustafa has a permutation <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(A\\\\)</span> contains all numbers <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(1\\\\)</span> to <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(n\\\\)</span>.</p><p>and <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(q\\\\)</span> queries each query with <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(l_i\\\\)</span> and <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(r_i\\\\)</span>.</p><p>for each query find the minimum positive value doesn't exist in the the subarray <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(A[l_i], A[l_{i + 1}], ....., A[r_i]\\\\)</span>.</p></div>", "inputSpec": "<p>The first line will contain only one integer <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(T\\\\)</span> <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(-\\\\)</span> the number of test cases.</p><p>Each test case will start with one line contain two integers <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(n\\\\)</span> and <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(q\\\\)</span>, (1 <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(\\\\leq\\\\)</span> <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(n, q\\\\)</span> <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(\\\\leq\\\\)</span> <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(10^5\\\\)</span>).</p><p>Follows <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(n\\\\)</span> numbers separated by a space representing the permutation <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(A\\\\)</span>.</p><p>Then <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(q\\\\)</span> lines follow each line contains <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(l_i\\\\)</span> and <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(r_i\\\\)</span> for the <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(i^{th}\\\\)</span> query.</p>", "testCases": [{"id": 1, "input": "2\\n6 6\\n2 6 1 5 3 4\\n1 6\\n1 5\\n1 3\\n4 6\\n5 5\\n3 3\\n4 10\\n4 2 1 3\\n1 1\\n1 2\\n2 2\\n1 3\\n2 3\\n3 3\\n1 4\\n2 4\\n3 4\\n4 4", "output": "7\\n4\\n3\\n1\\n1\\n2\\n1\\n1\\n1\\n3\\n3\\n2\\n5\\n4\\n2\\n1"}], "outputSpec": "<p>For each query print the minimum positive value doesn't exist in the subarray.</p>"}	\N	1000	372026
275	4	23	W	Encrypt & Decrypt Message	https://codeforces.com/group/MWSDmqGsZm/contest/219856/problem/W	{"meta": {"title": "W. Encrypt & Decrypt Message", "inputType": "standard input", "timeLimit": "1 second", "outputType": "standard output", "memoryLimit": "256 megabytes", "timeLimitMs": 1000, "memoryLimitMB": 256}, "note": null, "type": "problem", "story": "<div><p>Given a number <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(Q\\\\)</span> and a string <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(S\\\\)</span>. If <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(Q\\\\)</span> is equal to <span class=\\"tex-font-style-bf\\">1</span> then print <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(S\\\\)</span> after <span class=\\"tex-font-style-bf\\">encrypting</span> it otherwise, print <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(S\\\\)</span> after <span class=\\"tex-font-style-bf\\">decrypting</span> it.</p><p>Key = \\"PgEfTYaWGHjDAmxQqFLRpCJBownyUKZXkbvzIdshurMilNSVOtec#@_!=.+-*/\\".</p><p>Original = \\"abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ0123456789\\".</p><p><span class=\\"tex-font-style-bf\\">Note:</span> </p><ul> <li> In Encryption: For each letter <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(x\\\\)</span> in \\"<span class=\\"tex-font-style-bf\\">Original</span>\\" replace it by the equivalent letter <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(y\\\\)</span> from \\"<span class=\\"tex-font-style-bf\\">Key</span>\\"</li><li> In Decryption: For each letter <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(y\\\\)</span> in \\"<span class=\\"tex-font-style-bf\\">Key</span>\\" replace it by the equivalent letter <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(x\\\\)</span> from \\"<span class=\\"tex-font-style-bf\\">Original</span>\\".</li><li> Key and Original have the same length. </li></ul></div>", "inputSpec": "<p>The first line contains a number <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(Q\\\\)</span> <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\((1 \\\\le Q \\\\le 2)\\\\)</span>.</p><p>The second line contains a string <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(S\\\\)</span> <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(( 1 \\\\le |S| \\\\le 10^5)\\\\)</span> where |S| is the length of the string and it consists of <span class=\\"tex-font-style-bf\\">lowercase</span> and <span class=\\"tex-font-style-bf\\">uppercase</span> English letters.</p>", "testCases": [{"id": 1, "input": "1\\nEgypt", "output": "ZaoQR"}, {"id": 2, "input": "2\\n#@_!=.+-*/", "output": "0123456789"}, {"id": 3, "input": "2\\nZaoQR", "output": "Egypt"}], "outputSpec": "<p>Print the answer required above.</p>"}	\N	800	219856
276	15	3	C	Forms	https://codeforces.com/group/E23MsQv91X/contest/317001/problem/C	{"meta": {"title": "C. Forms", "inputType": "standard input", "timeLimit": "1 second", "outputType": "standard output", "memoryLimit": "256 megabytes", "timeLimitMs": 1000, "memoryLimitMB": 256}, "note": "<p>There are 4 formulas that can be obtained: </p><p>125, 1+25, 12+5, and 1+2+5.</p><p>When each formula is evaluated,125</p><p>1+25=26</p><p>12+5=17</p><p>1+2+5=8</p><p>Thus, the sum is 125+26+17+8=176.</p>", "type": "problem", "story": "<div><p>You are given a string S Consisting of digits between 1 and 9, inclusive. You can insert the letter + into some of the positions (possibly none) between two letters in this string. Here, + must not occur consecutively after insertion.</p><p>All strings that can be obtained in this way can be evaluated as formulas.</p><p>Evaluate all possible formulas, and print the sum of the results.</p></div>", "inputSpec": "<p>1≤|S|≤10 All letters in S are digits between 1 and 9, inclusive.</p>", "testCases": [{"id": 1, "input": "125", "output": "176"}], "outputSpec": "<p>Print the sum of the evaluated value over all possible formulas.</p>"}	\N	\N	317001
277	3	21	U	Is B a subsequence of A ?	https://codeforces.com/group/MWSDmqGsZm/contest/219774/problem/U	{"meta": {"title": "U. Is B a subsequence of A ?", "inputType": "standard input", "timeLimit": "1 second", "outputType": "standard output", "memoryLimit": "256 megabytes", "timeLimitMs": 1000, "memoryLimitMB": 256}, "note": null, "type": "problem", "story": "<div><p><span class=\\"tex-font-style-bf\\">a sub sequence</span> is a sequence that can be derived from another sequence by deleting some or no elements without changing the order of the remaining elements.</p><p>IF array = <span class=\\"tex-font-style-bf\\">[1,6,3 , 7]</span> then the <span class=\\"tex-font-style-bf\\">some subsequences</span> are <span class=\\"tex-font-style-bf\\"> [1,3,7] , [6,7] , [1] , [6,3,7] , [1,7] </span> . </p><p>Something like <span class=\\"tex-font-style-bf\\">[3,1]</span> and <span class=\\"tex-font-style-bf\\">[6 , 7 , 1]</span> would not be sub sequences of the array <span class=\\"tex-font-style-bf\\">[1,6,3 , 7]</span>.</p><p>Given <span class=\\"tex-font-style-bf\\">2</span> numbers <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(N\\\\)</span>, <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(M\\\\)</span> and <span class=\\"tex-font-style-bf\\">2</span> arrays <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(A\\\\)</span> consists of <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(N\\\\)</span> numbers and <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(B\\\\)</span> consists of <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(M\\\\)</span> numbers. Determine whether <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(B\\\\)</span> is a <span class=\\"tex-font-style-bf\\">sub-sequence</span> of <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(A\\\\)</span> or <span class=\\"tex-font-style-bf\\">not</span>.</p><p><span class=\\"tex-font-style-bf\\">Note:</span> The array <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(B\\\\)</span> is called a <span class=\\"tex-font-style-bf\\">sub-sequence</span> of <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(A\\\\)</span> if it's possible to <span class=\\"tex-font-style-bf\\">remove</span> zero or some elements from <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(A\\\\)</span> to get <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(B\\\\)</span>.</p><p><span class=\\"tex-font-style-bf\\">For example:</span> if <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(A\\\\)</span>=[<span class=\\"tex-font-style-bf\\">1,4,7</span>], and <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(B\\\\)</span> is [<span class=\\"tex-font-style-bf\\">1</span>], [<span class=\\"tex-font-style-bf\\">1,4</span>], [<span class=\\"tex-font-style-bf\\">1,7</span>],[<span class=\\"tex-font-style-bf\\">1,4,7</span>] or [<span class=\\"tex-font-style-bf\\">4,7</span>] then <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(B\\\\)</span> is a <span class=\\"tex-font-style-bf\\">sub-sequence</span> of <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(A\\\\)</span>.</p></div>", "inputSpec": "<p>First line contains two numbers <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(N, M\\\\)</span> <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\((1\\\\le N \\\\le 10^4, 1 \\\\le M \\\\le N)\\\\)</span> , the sizes of arrays <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(A\\\\)</span> and <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(B\\\\)</span> respectively.</p><p>Second line contains <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(N\\\\)</span> numbers <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\((1 \\\\le A_i \\\\le 10^9)\\\\)</span> elements of array <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(A\\\\)</span>.</p><p>Third line contains <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(M\\\\)</span> numbers <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\((1 \\\\le B_i \\\\le 10^9)\\\\)</span> elements of array <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(B\\\\)</span>.</p>", "testCases": [{"id": 1, "input": "3 2\\n1 4 7\\n1 7", "output": "YES"}, {"id": 2, "input": "7 4\\n1 8 4 7 5 2 7\\n4 5 7 2", "output": "NO"}, {"id": 3, "input": "3 3\\n21 8 40\\n21 8 40", "output": "YES"}], "outputSpec": "<p>Print \\"<span class=\\"tex-font-style-bf\\">YES</span>\\" (without the quotes), if <span class=\\"cf