pan>: change <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(n\\\\)</span> to <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(\\\\mathbin{\\\\sim}\\\\)</span><span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(n\\\\)</span> ,where <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(\\\\mathbin{\\\\sim}\\\\)</span> is bitwise <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(not\\\\)</span>. </li></ul></div>", "inputSpec": "<p>The first line of input contains two number <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(q,n\\\\)</span> <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\((1 \\\\le q \\\\le 10^5,-10^9 \\\\le n \\\\le 10^9)\\\\)</span>.</p><p>The next <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(q\\\\)</span> lines one type of query. <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\((-10^9 \\\\le x \\\\le 10^9)\\\\)</span>.</p>", "testCases": [{"id": 1, "input": "4 5\\n1 2\\n2 1\\n3 1\\n4", "output": "7\\n1\\n0\\n-1"}], "outputSpec": "<p>print <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(q\\\\)</span> lines, the <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(i^{th}\\\\)</span> line contains the value of <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(n\\\\)</span> after the <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(i^{th}\\\\)</span> update.</p>"}	\N	\N	267312
375	24	10	J	AND, OR and square sum	https://codeforces.com/group/3nQaj5GMG5/contest/377898/problem/J	{"meta": {"title": "J. AND, OR and square sum", "inputType": "standard input", "timeLimit": "2 seconds", "outputType": "standard output", "memoryLimit": "512 megabytes", "timeLimitMs": 2000, "memoryLimitMB": 512}, "note": "<p>In the first sample no operation can be made, thus the answer is <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(123^2\\\\)</span>.</p><p>In the second sample we can obtain the collection <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(1, 1, 7\\\\)</span>, and <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(1^2 + 1^2 + 7^2 = 51\\\\)</span>.</p><p>If <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(x\\\\)</span> and <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(y\\\\)</span> are represented in binary with equal number of bits (possibly with leading zeros), then each bit of <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(x~\\\\mathsf{AND}~y\\\\)</span> is set to <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(1\\\\)</span> if and only if both corresponding bits of <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(x\\\\)</span> and <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(y\\\\)</span> are set to <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(1\\\\)</span>. Similarly, each bit of <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(x~\\\\mathsf{OR}~y\\\\)</span> is set to <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(1\\\\)</span> if and only if at least one of the corresponding bits of <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(x\\\\)</span> and <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(y\\\\)</span> are set to <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(1\\\\)</span>. For example, <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(x = 3\\\\)</span> and <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(y = 5\\\\)</span> are represented as <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(011_2\\\\)</span> and <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(101_2\\\\)</span> (highest bit first). Then, <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(x~\\\\mathsf{AND}~y = 001_2 = 1\\\\)</span>, and <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(x~\\\\mathsf{OR}~y = 111_2 = 7\\\\)</span>.</p>", "type": "problem", "story": "<div><p>Gottfried learned about binary number representation. He then came up with this task and presented it to you.</p><p>You are given a collection of <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(n\\\\)</span> non-negative integers <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(a_1, \\\\ldots, a_n\\\\)</span>. You are allowed to perform the following operation: choose two distinct indices <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(1 \\\\leq i, j \\\\leq n\\\\)</span>. If before the operation <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(a_i = x\\\\)</span>, <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(a_j = y\\\\)</span>, then after the operation <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(a_i = x~\\\\mathsf{AND}~y\\\\)</span>, <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(a_j = x~\\\\mathsf{OR}~y\\\\)</span>, where <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(\\\\mathsf{AND}\\\\)</span> and <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(\\\\mathsf{OR}\\\\)</span> are bitwise AND and OR respectively (refer to the Notes section for formal description). The operation may be performed any number of times (possibly zero).</p><p>After all operations are done, compute <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(\\\\sum_{i=1}^n a_i^2\\\\)</span>&nbsp;— the sum of squares of all <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(a_i\\\\)</span>. What is the largest sum of squares you can achieve?</p></div>", "inputSpec": "<p>The first line contains a single integer <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(n\\\\)</span> (<span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(1 \\\\leq n \\\\leq 2 \\\\cdot 10^5\\\\)</span>).</p><p>The second line contains <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(n\\\\)</span> integers <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(a_1, \\\\ldots, a_n\\\\)</span> (<span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(0 \\\\leq a_i  \\\\lt  2^{20}\\\\)</span>).</p>", "testCases": [{"id": 1, "input": "1\\n123", "output": "15129"}, {"id": 2, "input": "3\\n1 3 5", "output": "51"}, {"id": 3, "input": "2\\n349525 699050", "output": "1099509530625"}], "outputSpec": "<p>Print a single integer&nbsp;— the largest possible sum of squares that can be achieved after several (possibly zero) operations.</p>"}	\N	1700	377898
