384	33	14	N	Merge Intervals	https://codeforces.com/group/c3FDl9EUi9/contest/262795/problem/N	{"meta": {"title": "N. Merge Intervals", "inputType": "standard input", "timeLimit": "1 second", "outputType": "standard output", "memoryLimit": "256 megabytes", "timeLimitMs": 1000, "memoryLimitMB": 256}, "note": null, "type": "problem", "story": "<div><p>You have <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(N\\\\)</span> intervals of integers, each of them has numbers from to <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\([l:r]\\\\)</span>.</p><p>and we need to minimize the number of these intervals by using this operation :</p><p>choose any two intervals <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(a,b\\\\)</span> - such that <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(a\\\\)</span> and <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(b\\\\)</span> intersect with each other - and remove them, then add a new interval <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(c\\\\)</span> has all the numbers in <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(a\\\\)</span> and <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(b\\\\)</span> only.</p><p>you can use this operation any number of times.</p></div>", "inputSpec": "<p>The first line of input contains <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(N\\\\)</span> <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\((1 \\\\le N \\\\le 10^5)\\\\)</span>.</p><p>Then <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(N\\\\)</span> lines, the <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(i_{th}\\\\)</span> line contains <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(l_i\\\\)</span> , <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(r_i\\\\)</span> <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\((1 \\\\le l_i , r_i \\\\le 10^9)\\\\)</span></p>", "testCases": [{"id": 1, "input": "5\\n2 4\\n9 12\\n6 9\\n8 10\\n1 3", "output": "1 4\\n6 12"}], "outputSpec": "<p>print the new intervals in separate lines sorted according to minimum <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(l\\\\)</span>.</p>"}	\N	\N	262795
