pan class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(q\\\\)</span> lines contains <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(x1,y1,x2,y2 (1 \\\\leq x1 \\\\leq x2 \\\\leq 10^9, 1 \\\\leq y1 \\\\leq y2 \\\\leq 10^9)\\\\)</span>.</p>", "testCases": [{"id": 1, "input": "5 4\\n1 3 4\\n2 2 6\\n4 3 3\\n5 4 8\\n5 6 5\\n1 1 2 3\\n2 2 4 5\\n2 3 6 4\\n1 3 5 6", "output": "10\\n9\\n11\\n20"}], "outputSpec": "<p>For each query print the answer of this query in one line.</p>"}	\N	\N	374321
447	25	3	C	Solve Equation	https://codeforces.com/group/c3FDl9EUi9/contest/264941/problem/C	{"meta": {"title": "C. Solve Equation", "inputType": "standard input", "timeLimit": "1 second", "outputType": "standard output", "memoryLimit": "256 megabytes", "timeLimitMs": 1000, "memoryLimitMB": 256}, "note": null, "type": "problem", "story": "<div><p>You have implemented a sorting algorithm that requires exactly <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(c*n*lg(n)\\\\)</span> nanoseconds to sort <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(n\\\\)</span> integers. Here <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(lg\\\\)</span> denotes the base-2 logarithm. </p><p>Given <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(time\\\\)</span> in nanoseconds, print the largest value of <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(n\\\\)</span> such that <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(c \\\\times n \\\\times lg(n) \\\\le time\\\\)</span>.</p></div>", "inputSpec": "<p>only one line contains two integers <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(c\\\\)</span>, <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(time\\\\)</span> (<span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(1\\\\)</span> <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(\\\\le\\\\)</span> <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(c\\\\)</span> <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(\\\\le\\\\)</span> <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(100\\\\)</span>),(<span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(1\\\\)</span> <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(\\\\le\\\\)</span> <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(time\\\\)</span> <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(\\\\le\\\\)</span> <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(2\\\\)</span> <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(\\\\times\\\\)</span> <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(10^9\\\\)</span>).</p>", "testCases": [{"id": 1, "input": "1 8", "output": "4.000000"}, {"id": 2, "input": "2 16", "output": "4.000000"}, {"id": 3, "input": "37 12392342", "output": "23104.999312"}, {"id": 4, "input": "1 2000000000", "output": "76374950.903478"}], "outputSpec": "<p>print in one line the largest value of <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(n\\\\)</span>.</p><p>Your answer is considered correct if its absolute or relative error does not exceed <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(10^{-6}\\\\)</span>. Formally, let your answer be <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(a\\\\)</span>, and the jury's answer be <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(b\\\\)</span>. Your answer is accepted if and only if <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(\\\\frac{|a - b|}{\\\\max{(1, |b|)}} \\\\le 10^{-6}\\\\)</span>.</p>"}	\N	\N	264941
448	24	4	D	Preparing Olympiad	https://codeforces.com/group/3nQaj5GMG5/contest/377898/problem/D	{"meta": {"title": "D. Preparing Olympiad", "inputType": "standard input", "timeLimit": "2 seconds", "outputType": "standard output", "memoryLimit": "256 megabytes", "timeLimitMs": 2000, "memoryLimitMB": 256}, "note": "<p>In the first example two sets are suitable, one consisting of the second and third problem, another one consisting of all three problems.</p><p>In the second example, two sets of problems are suitable — the set of problems with difficulties 10 and 30 as well as the set of problems with difficulties 20 and 30.</p><p>In the third example any set consisting of one problem of difficulty 10 and one problem of difficulty 20 is suitable.</p>", "type": "problem", "story": "<div><p>You have <span class=\\"tex-span\\"><i>n</i></span> problems. You have estimated the difficulty of the <span class=\\"tex-span\\"><i>i</i></span>-th one as integer <span class=\\"tex-span\\"><i>c</i><sub class=\\"lower-index\\"><i>i</i></sub></span>. Now you want to prepare a problemset for a contest, using some of the problems you've made.</p><p>A problemset for the contest must consist of at least two problems. You think that the total difficulty of the problems of the contest must be at least <span class=\\"tex-span\\"><i>l</i></span> and at most <span class=\\"tex-span\\"><i>r</i></span>. Also, you think that the difference between difficulties of the easiest and the hardest of the chosen problems must be at least <span class=\\"tex-span\\"><i>x</i></span>.</p><p>Find the number of ways to choose a problemset for the contest.</p></div>", "inputSpec": "<p>The first line contains four integers <span class=\\"tex-span\\"><i>n</i></span>, <span class=\\"tex-span\\"><i>l</i></span>, <span class=\\"tex-span\\"><i>r</i></span>, <span class=\\"tex-span\\"><i>x</i></span> (<span class=\\"tex-span\\">1 ≤ <i>n</i> ≤ 15</span>, <span class=\\"tex-span\\">1 ≤ <i>l</i> ≤ <i>r</i> ≤ 10<sup class=\\"upper-index\\">9</sup></span>, <span class=\\"tex-span\\">1 ≤ <i>x</i> ≤ 10<sup class=\\"upper-index\\">6</sup></span>) — the number of problems you have, the minimum and maximum value of total difficulty of the problemset and the minimum difference in difficulty between the hardest problem in the pack and the easiest one, respectively.</p><p>The second line contains <span class=\\"tex-span\\"><i>n</i></span> integers <span class=\\"tex-span\\"><i>c</i><sub class=\\"lower-index\\">1</sub>, <i>c</i><sub class=\\"lower-index\\">2</sub>, ..., <i>c</i><sub class=\\"lower-index\\"><i>n</i></sub></span> (<span class=\\"tex-span\\">1 ≤ <i>c</i><sub class=\\"lower-index\\"><i>i</i></sub> ≤ 10<sup class=\\"upper-index\\">6</sup></span>) — the difficulty of each problem.</p>", "testCases": [{"id": 1, "input": "3 5 6 1\\n1 2 3", "output": "2"}, {"id": 2, "input": "4 40 50 10\\n10 20 30 25", "output": "2"}, {"id": 3, "input": "5 25 35 10\\n10 10 20 10 20", "output": "6"}], "outputSpec": "<p>Print the number of ways to choose a suitable problemset for the contest. </p>"}	\N	1400	377898
449	24	8	H	Compiler_101	https://codeforces.com/group/3nQaj5GMG5/contest/377898/problem/H	{"meta": {"title": "H. Compiler_101", "inputType": "standard input", "timeLimit": "2 seconds", "outputType": "standard output", "memoryLimit": "256 megabytes", "timeLimitMs": 2000, "memoryLimitMB": 256}, "note": null, "type": "problem", "story": "<div><p>Compiler_101 read a book about bitwise operation and learned that the value of the subarray [L,R] is equal to <span class=\\"tex-span\\"><i>F</i>(<i>L</i>, <i>R</i>)</span>.</p><p>Where <span class=\\"tex-span\\"><i>F</i>(<i>L</i>, <i>R</i>)</span> is calculated as an operation of bitwise OR of all the elements with indexes from L to R. Formally: <span class=\\"tex-span\\"><i>F</i>(<i>L</i>,  <i>R</i>)  =  <i>a</i><sub class=\\"lower-index\\"><i>L</i></sub></span> <span class=\\"tex-span\\">|</span> <span class=\\"tex-span\\"><i>a</i><sub class=\\"lower-index\\"><i>L</i> + 1</sub></span> <span class=\\"tex-span\\">|</span> <span class=\\"tex-span\\">...</span> <span class=\\"tex-span\\">|</span> <span class=\\"tex-span\\"><i>a</i><sub class=\\"lower-index\\"><i>R</i></sub></span>.</p><p>One day he got an array a of length <span class=\\"tex-span\\"><i>n</i></span> and wondered what is the smallest length of <span class=\\"tex-font-style-bf\\">non-empty</span> contiguous subarray where the value is maximal.</p></div>", "inputSpec": "<p>The first line contains <span class=\\"tex-span\\"><i>n</i></span> <span class=\\"tex-span\\">(1 ≤ <i>n</i> ≤ 3×10<sup class=\\"upper-index\\">5</sup>)</span></p><p>The second line contains <span class=\\"tex-span\\"><i>n</i></span> space separated integers, the array <span class=\\"tex-span\\"><i>a</i></span> <span class=\\"tex-span\\">(0 ≤ <i>a</i><sub class=\\"lower-index\\"><i>i</i></sub> ≤ 10<sup class=\\"upper-index\\">9</sup>)</span></p>", "testCases": [{"id": 1, "input": "5\\n0 3 0 4 0", "output": "3"}], "outputSpec": "<p>single integer the subarray length.</p>"}	\N	\N	377898
450	9	3	C	Dragons	https://codeforces.com/group/MWSDmqGsZm/contest/223207/problem/C	{"meta": {"title": "C. Dragons", "inputType": "stdin", "timeLimit": "2 seconds", "outputType": "stdout", "memoryLimit": "256 megabytes", "timeLimitMs": 2000, "memoryLimitMB": 256}, "note": "<p>In the first sample Kirito's strength initially equals 2. As the first dragon's strength is less than 2, Kirito can fight it and defeat it. After that he gets the bonus and his strength increases to <span class=\\"tex-span\\">2 + 99 = 101</span>. Now he can defeat the second dragon and move on to the next level.</p><p>In the second sample Kirito's strength is too small to defeat the only dragon and win.</p>", "type": "problem", "story": "<div><p>Kirito is stuck on a level of the MMORPG he is playing now. To move on in the game, he's got to defeat all <span class=\\"tex-span\\"><i>n</i></span> dragons that live on this level. Kirito and the dragons have <span class=\\"tex-font-style-underline\\">strength</span>, which is represented by an integer. In the duel between two opponents the duel's outcome is determined by their strength. Initially, Kirito's strength equals <span class=\\"tex-span\\"><i>s</i></span>.</p><p>If Kirito starts duelling with the <span class=\\"tex-span\\"><i>i</i></span>-th (<span class=\\"tex-span\\">1 ≤ <i>i</i> ≤ <i>n</i></span>) dragon and Kirito's strength is not greater than the dragon's strength <span class=\\"tex-span\\"><i>x</i><sub class=\\"lower-index\\"><i>i</i></sub></span>, then Kirito loses the duel and dies. But if Kirito's strength is greater than the dragon's strength, then he defeats the dragon and gets a bonus strength increase by <span class=\\"tex-span\\"><i>y</i><sub class=\\"lower-index\\"><i>i</i></sub></span>.</p><p>Kirito can fight the dragons in any order. Determine whether he can move on to the next level of the game, that is, defeat all dragons without a single loss.</p></div>", "inputSpec": "<p>The first line contains two space-separated integers <span class=\\"tex-span\\"><i>s</i></span> and <span class=\\"tex-span\\"><i>n</i></span> (<span class=\\"tex-span\\">1 ≤ <i>s</i> ≤ 10<sup class=\\"upper-index\\">4</sup></span>, <span class=\\"tex-span\\">1 ≤ <i>n</i> ≤ 10<sup class=\\"upper-index\\">3</sup></span>). Then <span class=\\"tex-span\\"><i>n</i></span> lines follow: the <span class=\\"tex-span\\"><i>i</i></span>-th line contains space-separated integers <span class=\\"tex-span\\"><i>x</i><sub class=\\"lower-index\\"><i>i</i></sub></span> and <span class=\\"tex-span\\"><i>y</i><sub class=\\"lower-index\\"><i>i</i></sub></span> (<span class=\\"tex-span\\">1 ≤ <i>x</i><sub class=\\"lower-index\\"><i>i</i></sub> ≤ 10<sup class=\\"upper-index\\">4</sup></span>, <span class=\\"tex-span\\">0 ≤ <i>y</i><sub class=\\"lower-index\\"><i>i</i></sub> ≤ 10<sup class=\\"upper-index\\">4</sup></span>) — the <span class=\\"tex-span\\"><i>i</i></span>-th dragon's strength and the bonus for defeating it.</p>", "testCases": [{"id": 1, "input": "2 2\\n1 99\\n100 0", "output": "YES"}, {"id": 2, "input": "10 1\\n100 100", "output": "NO"}], "outputSpec": "<p>On a single line print \\"<span class=\\"tex-font-style-tt\\">YES</span>\\" (without the quotes), if Kirito can move on to the next level and print \\"<span class=\\"tex-font-style-tt\\">NO</span>\\" (without the quotes), if he can't.</p>"}	\N	1000	223207
451	6	21	U	Straight Line	https://codeforces.com/group/MWSDmqGsZm/contest/223338/problem/U	{"meta": {"title": "U. Straight Line", "inputType": "standard input", "timeLimit": "1 second", "outputType": "standard output", "memoryLimit": "256 megabytes", "timeLimitMs": 1000, "memoryLimitMB": 256}, "note": null, "type": "problem", "story": "<div><p>Given three points on the Cartesian plane. Determine whether a single straight line can pass through these points or not.</p></div>", "inputSpec": "<p>First line contains two numbers <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(X_1, Y_1\\\\)</span> <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\((-10^5 \\\\leq X_1,Y_1 \\\\leq 10^5)\\\\)</span>.</p><p>Second line contains two numbers <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(X_2, Y_2\\\\)</span> <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\((-10^5 \\\\leq X_2,Y_2 \\\\leq 10^5)\\\\)</span>.</p><p>Third line contains two numbers <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(X_3, Y_3\\\\)</span> <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\((-10^5 \\\\leq X_3,Y_3 \\\\leq 10^5)\\\\)</span>.</p>", "testCases": [{"id": 1, "input": "1 1\\n2 2\\n3 3", "output": "YES"}, {"id": 2, "input": "0 1\\n-4 7\\n3 3", "output": "NO"}], "outputSpec": "<p>Print \\"<span class=\\"tex-font-style-bf\\">YES</span>\\" if a single straight line can pass through the three points otherwise, print \\"<span class=\\"tex-font-style-bf\\">NO</span>\\".</p>"}	\N	800	223338
