453	23	3	C	Bitmask Operation (hard)	https://codeforces.com/group/c3FDl9EUi9/contest/267312/problem/C	{"meta": {"title": "C. Bitmask Operation (hard)", "inputType": "standard input", "timeLimit": "1 second", "outputType": "standard output", "memoryLimit": "256 megabytes", "timeLimitMs": 1000, "memoryLimitMB": 256}, "note": null, "type": "problem", "story": "<div><p>You have a number <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(n\\\\)</span> (32 bit signed integer) and <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(q\\\\)</span> queries. </p><ul> <li> <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(1\\\\)</span>: change value of (first bit equal to <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(0\\\\)</span>) to <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(1\\\\)</span>. </li><li> <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(2\\\\)</span>: change value of (first bit equal to <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(1\\\\)</span>) to <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(0\\\\)</span>. </li><li> <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(3\\\\)</span>: change all bits (from index <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(0\\\\)</span> until first bit equal to <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(1\\\\)</span>) to <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(1\\\\)</span>. if <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(n\\\\)</span> equal 0,then <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(n\\\\)</span> will be <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(-1\\\\)</span>. </li><li> <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(4\\\\)</span>: change all bits (from index <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(0\\\\)</span> until first bit equal to <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(0\\\\)</span>) to <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(0\\\\)</span>. </li><li> <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(5\\\\)</span>: if <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(n\\\\)</span> is power of two print \\"is power of two\\", otherwise print \\"not power of two\\". </li></ul></div>", "inputSpec": "<p>The first line of input contains two number <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(n,q\\\\)</span> <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\((0 &lt; n \\\\le 10^9,1 \\\\le q \\\\le 10^5)\\\\)</span>.</p><p>The next <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(q\\\\)</span> lines one type of query.</p>", "testCases": [{"id": 1, "input": "5 7\\n1\\n2\\n3\\n5\\n4\\n1\\n5", "output": "7\\n6\\n7\\nnot power of two\\n0\\n1\\nis power of two"}], "outputSpec": "<p>print <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(q\\\\)</span> lines, each query in one line. if query from type 5 just answers the query, otherwise print the value of <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(n\\\\)</span> after changes.</p>"}	\N	\N	267312
454	27	3	C	The Grades	https://codeforces.com/group/c3FDl9EUi9/contest/263722/problem/C	{"meta": {"title": "C. The Grades", "inputType": "standard input", "timeLimit": "1 second", "outputType": "standard output", "memoryLimit": "256 megabytes", "timeLimitMs": 1000, "memoryLimitMB": 256}, "note": null, "type": "problem", "story": "<div><p>You have <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(N\\\\)</span> friends each of them you know his name and the grades of Arabic, Maths, Science, and English.</p><p>you need to sort your friends according to these conditions: </p><ul> <li> If the absolute difference between the total grades is greater than 10, then you have to put the person with a higher grade in the first. </li><li> Otherwise you have to compare their names such that the friend with the smallest lexicographically name will be in the first. </li></ul></div>", "inputSpec": "<p>The first line of input an contains integer <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(N\\\\)</span> <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\((1 \\\\leq N \\\\leq 10^5)\\\\)</span>.</p><p>Then next <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(N\\\\)</span> lines, the <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(i_{th}\\\\)</span> line contains string <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(Name\\\\)</span> <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\((1 \\\\leq |Name| \\\\leq 10)\\\\)</span> the name of the <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(i_{th}\\\\)</span> firnd,its guaranted that all <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(N\\\\)</span> names are distncet, and Four integers <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(A\\\\)</span>,<span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(M\\\\)</span>,<span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(S\\\\)</span>,<span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(E\\\\)</span> <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\((1 \\\\leq A,M,S,E \\\\leq 100)\\\\)</span> the grades of Arabic, Maths, Science, and English respectively of the <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(i_{th}\\\\)</span> frind.</p>", "testCases": [{"id": 1, "input": "7\\nHussien 95 75 65 85\\nHafez 98 57 75 68\\nOmar 77 68 75 64\\nAtef 56 97 75 94\\nKaremo 60 91 98 70\\nEzzat 72 83 69 95\\nMuhammad 98 97 57 95", "output": "Muhammad 347 98 97 57 95\\nAtef 322 56 97 75 94\\nEzzat 319 72 83 69 95\\nHussien 320 95 75 65 85\\nKaremo 319 60 91 98 70\\nHafez 298 98 57 75 68\\nOmar 284 77 68 75 64"}], "outputSpec": "<p>Print <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(N\\\\)</span> lines, the <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(i_{th}\\\\)</span> contains the name and the grades of Arabic, Maths, Science, and English of the <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(i_{th}\\\\)</span> friend in this order after the sorting.</p>"}	\N	\N	263722
455	9	12	L	Announcement !	https://codeforces.com/group/MWSDmqGsZm/contest/223207/problem/L	{"meta": {"title": "L. Announcement !", "inputType": "standard input", "timeLimit": "1 second", "outputType": "standard output", "memoryLimit": "256 megabytes", "timeLimitMs": 1000, "memoryLimitMB": 256}, "note": null, "type": "problem", "story": "<div><p>During the last contest, There was a notification saying \\"2 Problems are added Enjoy\\" Yasser found that the contestants were angry.</p><p>After the contest Moamen gives Yasser the problems of the next contest and asked him if the difficulty level of any problem exists more than once he will replace it with another easy problem.</p><p>Given <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(N\\\\)</span> (The number of problems) then the difficulty of each problem and find How many problems should be replaced? If each problem exists exactly once print -1</p></div>", "inputSpec": "<p>The first line of the input contains one Number <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(N\\\\)</span> <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\((1 \\\\le N \\\\le 10^4)\\\\)</span> </p><p>followed by <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(N\\\\)</span> numbers -The difficulty level of the problems- <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\((0 \\\\le level \\\\le 10^6)\\\\)</span> </p>", "testCases": [{"id": 1, "input": "3\\n1 1 2", "output": "1"}, {"id": 2, "input": "1\\n1", "output": "-1"}, {"id": 3, "input": "5\\n1 2 3 4 3", "output": "1"}, {"id": 4, "input": "4\\n1 1 3 3", "output": "2"}], "outputSpec": "<p>Print the answer of the problem.</p>"}	\N	\N	223207
456	21	3	C	Maximum in Subarrays	https://codeforces.com/group/E23MsQv91X/contest/311232/problem/C	{"meta": {"title": "C. Maximum in Subarrays", "inputType": "standard input", "timeLimit": "1 second", "outputType": "standard output", "memoryLimit": "256 megabytes", "timeLimitMs": 1000, "memoryLimitMB": 256}, "note": null, "type": "problem", "story": "<div><p>given array of size n and you need to calculate this formula : </p><center> .<span><span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(\\\\displaystyle\\\\sum_{i=1}^{n} \\\\sum_{j=i}^{n} max(i,j)\\\\)</span></span> </center> where <span class=\\"tex-font-style-bf\\"><span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(max(i,j)\\\\)</span></span> is maximum element in subarray <span class=\\"tex-font-style-bf\\"><span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(i\\\\)</span></span> to <span class=\\"tex-font-style-bf\\"><span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(j\\\\)</span></span>.<p>in other word you need to calculate summation of maximum element in all subarrays <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(i\\\\)</span> and <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(j\\\\)</span> <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\((1 \\\\le i \\\\le j \\\\le n)\\\\)</span>.</p></div>", "inputSpec": "<p>the first line contains one integer <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(n (1 \\\\le n \\\\le 10^6)\\\\)</span> , the size of array.</p><p>The second line contains <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(n\\\\)</span> distinct numbers <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(a_i (1 \\\\le a_i \\\\le 10^7)\\\\)</span>.</p>", "testCases": [{"id": 1, "input": "5\\n10 3 1 5 2", "output": "89"}, {"id": 2, "input": "4\\n1 6 3 4", "output": "48"}], "outputSpec": "<p>Print one integer, the result of formula.</p>"}	\N	\N	311232
457	9	14	N	Pumbaa And Apples	https://codeforces.com/group/MWSDmqGsZm/contest/223207/problem/N	{"meta": {"title": "N. Pumbaa And Apples", "inputType": "standard input", "timeLimit": "1 second", "outputType": "standard output", "memoryLimit": "256 megabytes", "timeLimitMs": 1000, "memoryLimitMB": 256}, "note": "<p>Let's see how the farm changes in the second test case.</p><p>After the first instruction is fulfilled, the table looks like that:</p><p>2 1 4</p><p>1 3 5</p><p>After the second instruction is fulfilled, the table looks like that:</p><p>1 3 5</p><p>2 1 4</p><p>So the answer to the third instruction (the number located in the first row and in the third column) will be 5.</p>", "type": "problem", "story": "<div><p><span class=\\"tex-font-style-bf\\">Pop</span> stores some secret information about a farm with <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(n * m\\\\)</span> apples represents a rectangle. Each apple has it's own number. The order of apples in the farm is changing. That's why <span class=\\"tex-font-style-bf\\">Pop</span> receives the following instructions:</p><p>-The instruction to swap two rows of the farm;</p><p>-The instruction to swap two columns of the farm;</p><p>-The instruction to obtain the number of the apple that exists in some cell.</p><p>As <span class=\\"tex-font-style-bf\\">Pop</span> is not clever, he asked <span class=\\"tex-font-style-bf\\">Alice</span> to execute these instructions.</p></div>", "inputSpec": "<p>The first line contains three space-separated integers <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(n\\\\)</span>, <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(m\\\\)</span> and <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(k\\\\)</span> <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\((1 ≤ n, m ≤ 1000, 1 ≤ k ≤ 10^6)\\\\)</span> — the number of farm rows and columns and the number of instructions, correspondingly.</p><p>Next <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(n\\\\)</span> lines contain <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(m\\\\)</span> space-separated numbers each — the initial state of the farm. Each number <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(p\\\\)</span> in the table is an integer and satisfies the inequality <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\((0 ≤ p ≤ 10^6)\\\\)</span>.</p><p>Next <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(k\\\\)</span> lines contain instructions in the format \\"<span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(s_i\\\\)</span> <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(x_i\\\\)</span> <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(y_i\\\\)</span>\\", where <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(s_i\\\\)</span> is one of the characters \\"<span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(с\\\\)</span>\\", \\"<span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(r\\\\)</span>\\" or \\"<span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(g\\\\)</span>\\", and <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(x_i\\\\)</span>, <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(y_i\\\\)</span> are two integers.</p><p>-If <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(s_i\\\\)</span> = \\"<span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(c\\\\)</span>\\", then the current instructions is to swap columns with indexes <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(x_i\\\\)</span> and <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(y_i\\\\)</span> <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\((1 ≤ x, y ≤ m, x ≠ y)\\\\)</span>;</p><p>-If <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(s_i\\\\)</span> = \\"<span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(r\\\\)</span>\\", then the current instruction is to swap rows with indexes <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(x_i\\\\)</span> and <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(y_i\\\\)</span> <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\((1 ≤ x, y ≤ n, x ≠ y)\\\\)</span>;</p><p>-If <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(s_i\\\\)</span> = \\"<span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(g\\\\)</span>\\", then the current instruction is to obtain the number that located in the <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(x_{th}\\\\)</span> row and in the <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(y_{th}\\\\)</span> column <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\((1 ≤ x ≤ n, 1 ≤ y ≤ m)\\\\)</span>.</p><p>The farm rows are considered to be indexed from top to bottom from 1 to <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(n\\\\)</span>, and the farm columns — from left to right from 1 to <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(m\\\\)</span>.</p>", "testCases": [{"id": 1, "input": "3 3 5\\n1 2 3\\n4 5 6\\n7 8 9\\ng 3 2\\nr 3 2\\nc 2 3\\ng 2 2\\ng 3 2", "output": "8\\n9\\n6"}, {"id": 2, "input": "2 3 3\\n1 2 4\\n3 1 5\\nc 2 1\\nr 1 2\\ng 1 3", "output": "5"}], "outputSpec": "<p>For each instruction to obtain a number <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\((s_i = \\"g\\")\\\\)</span> print the required number. Print the answers to the instructions in the order of the instruction in the input.</p>"}	\N	\N	223207
458	26	5	E	Truffula Trouble	https://codeforces.com/group/3nQaj5GMG5/contest/376466/problem/E	{"meta": {"title": "E. Truffula Trouble", "inputType": "standard input", "timeLimit": "1 second", "outputType": "standard output", "memoryLimit": "256 megabytes", "timeLimitMs": 1000, "memoryLimitMB": 256}, "note": "<p>In the first example, the Once-ler starts with durability <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(d=3\\\\)</span>, and chops down the 3rd and 5th trees to create 2 Thneeds.</p><p>In the second example, the Once-ler cannot make 5 Thneeds without angering the Lorax.</p>", "type": "problem", "story": "<div><p>The Once-ler is back with his lucrative Thneed business!</p><p>There are <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(N\\\\)</span> truffula trees in a row, and the Once-ler visits them <span class=\\"tex-font-style-bf\\">in order</span>, starting at the first truffula tree. He starts with a Super-Axe-Hacker with durability <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(d\\\\)</span>.</p><p>Each truffula tree has toughness <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(t_i\\\\)</span>, and the Once-ler can choose to chop down a truffula tree if and only if the durability of his Super-Axe-Hacker is greater than or equal to the current tree's toughness (<span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(d \\\\ge t_i\\\\)</span>). Every time the Once-ler chops down a tree, the durability of his Super-Axe-Hacker decreases by one.</p><p>However, this time, the Once-ler wants to avoid chopping down trees unsustainably and angering the Lorax. Therefore, the Once-ler refuses to chop down more than one tree in a row.</p><p>However, he still needs to make a profit. Each truffula tree he cuts down can make one Thneed. To reach his quota, he needs to make <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(k\\\\)</span> Thneeds.</p><p>What is the minimum starting durability <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(d_{min}\\\\)</span> of the Once-ler's Super-Axe-Hacker that guarantees at least <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(k\\\\)</span> Thneeds will be made?</p></div>", "inputSpec": "<p>The first line contains two integers <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(N\\\\)</span> and <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(k\\\\)</span> where <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(N\\\\)</span> is the number of truffula trees, and <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(k\\\\)</span> is the number of Thneeds the Once-ler needs to make. (<span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(1 \\\\le N \\\\le 10^5, 1 \\\\le k \\\\le N\\\\)</span>)</p><p>The next line contains <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(N\\\\)</span> integers <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(t_1...t_n\\\\)</span> where <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(t_i\\\\)</span> is the toughness of the <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(i\\\\)</span>th truffula tree. (<span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(1 \\\\le t_i \\\\le 10^9\\\\)</span>)</p>", "testCases": [{"id": 1, "input": "6 2\\n4 9 2 1 2 10", "output": "3"}, {"id": 2, "input": "6 5\\n8 8 8 8 8 8", "output": "-1"}], "outputSpec": "<p>Output <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(d_{min}\\\\)</span>, the minimum starting durability that guarantees at least <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(k\\\\)</span> Thneeds will be made. If it is not possible to make <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(k\\\\)</span> Thneeds while satisfying all the requirements, output <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(-1\\\\)</span>.</p>"}	\N	\N	376466
