619	17	3	C	Abdelkader and Hammouri	https://codeforces.com/group/E23MsQv91X/contest/315226/problem/C	{"meta": {"title": "C. Abdelkader and Hammouri", "inputType": "standard input", "timeLimit": "0.5 seconds", "outputType": "standard output", "memoryLimit": "64 megabytes", "timeLimitMs": 500, "memoryLimitMB": 64}, "note": null, "type": "problem", "story": "<div><p>Abdelkader and Hammouri want to paint a fence of <span class=\\"tex-span\\"><i>N</i></span> boards with black and white such that no two adjacent boards have the same color.</p><center> <img class=\\"tex-graphics\\" src=\\"https://espresso.codeforces.com/5781ba2c5856bebf8d10adf2171f755b3b37f007.png\\" style=\\"zoom: 70.0%;max-width: 100.0%;max-height: 100.0%;\\"> </center><p>Abdelkader will start painting from the left side with one of the colors, then each time will use different color than the last used one. Hammouri will start from the right side in the same way, but he wants to know the color with which he should start painting so that when they meet, no two adjacent boards will have the same color.</p></div>", "inputSpec": "<p>The first line of input contains a single integer <span class=\\"tex-span\\"><i>N</i></span> <span class=\\"tex-span\\">(2 ≤ <i>N</i> ≤ 10<sup class=\\"upper-index\\">9</sup>)</span>, the number of boards.</p><p>The second line contains the color Abdelkader will use at the beginning, \\"Black\\" or \\"White\\".</p>", "testCases": [{"id": 1, "input": "2\\nBlack", "output": "White"}, {"id": 2, "input": "32\\nWhite", "output": "Black"}], "outputSpec": "<p>Print \\"Black\\" or \\"White\\", the color Hammouri should start with.</p>"}	\N	\N	315226
620	17	7	G	smallest subsequence	https://codeforces.com/group/E23MsQv91X/contest/315226/problem/G	{"meta": {"title": "G. smallest subsequence", "inputType": "standard input", "timeLimit": "1 second", "outputType": "standard output", "memoryLimit": "256 megabytes", "timeLimitMs": 1000, "memoryLimitMB": 256}, "note": null, "type": "problem", "story": "<div><p>given string s, print the smallest lexicographically subsequence of s that contains all the distinct characters of s exactly once.</p><p>A subsequence is a sequence that can be derived from the given sequence by deleting zero or more elements without changing the order of the remaining elements.</p><p>for example <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\((\\"a\\",\\"b\\",\\"c\\",\\"ab\\",\\"ac\\",\\"bc\\",\\"abc\\")\\\\)</span> all are subsequence from <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\(\\"abc\\"\\\\)</span>, but <span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\((\\"ca\\",\\"cb\\",\\"ba\\")\\\\)</span> are not subsequence because the order are changed.</p></div>", "inputSpec": "<p>one line contains string s (<span class=\\"cf-inline-math\\">\\\\( 1 \\\\le |s| \\\\le 10^5 \\\\)</span>), consisting of lowercase Latin letters.</p>", "testCases": [{"id": 1, "input": "ecbacba", "output": "eacb"}, {"id": 2, "input": "cdadabcc", "output": "adbc"}], "outputSpec": "<p>one line contains answer of the problem.</p>"}	\N	\N	315226
621	2	7	G	Factorial	https://codeforces.com/group/MWSDmqGsZm/contest/219432/problem/G	{"meta": {"title": "G. Factorial", "inputType": "standard input", "timeLimit": "2 seconds", "outputType": "standard output", "memoryLimit": "64 megabytes", "timeLimitMs": 2000, "memoryLimitMB": 64}, "note": "<p><span class=\\"tex-font-style-bf\\">Factorial</span>, in mathematics, the product of all positive integers less than or equal to a given positive integer and denoted by that integer and an exclamation point.</p><p>Thus, factorial seven is written 7!, meaning <span class=\\"tex-font-style-bf\\">1 * 2 * 3 * 4 * 5 * 6 * 7 = 5040</span> . </p><p><span class=\\"tex-font-style-bf\\">Factorial zero is defined as equal to 1</span>.</p><p>In first test case for N = 5 , <span class=\\"tex-font-style-bf\\">5! = 1 * 2 * 3 * 4 * 5 = 120</span> so the answer is <span class=\\"tex-font-style-bf\\">120</span>.</p><p>In Second test case for N = 3 , <span class=\\"tex-font-style-bf\\">3! = 1 * 2 * 3 = 6</span> so the answer is <span class=\\"tex-font-style-bf\\">6</span>.</p>", "type": "problem", "story": "<div><p>Given a number <span class=\\"tex-span\\"><i>N</i></span>. Print the <span class=\\"tex-font-style-bf\\">factorial</span> of number <span class=\\"tex-span\\"><i>N</i></span>.</p></div>", "inputSpec": "<p>First line contains a number <span class=\\"tex-span\\"><i>T</i></span> <span class=\\"tex-span\\">(1 ≤ <i>T</i> ≤ 15)</span> number of test cases.</p><p>Next T lines will contain a number <span class=\\"tex-span\\"><i>N</i></span> <span class=\\"tex-span\\">(0 ≤ <i>N</i> ≤ 20)</span></p>", "testCases": [{"id": 1, "input": "2\\n5\\n3", "output": "120\\n6"}], "outputSpec": "<p>For each test case print a single line contains the <span class=\\"tex-font-style-bf\\">factorial</span> of <span class=\\"tex-span\\"><i>N</i></span>.</p>"}	\N	1300	219432
